findings.body:
`formatStudiesText` formats `strings.detailTextStudies`, which is the v1 copy ("may install and run studies from time to time"). The PR adds `detailTextStudiesV2` with the new "randomly selects users" wording, so this helper contradicts the new copy it sits next to. Nothing calls it yet, but a future caller would silently get the old text.

::code{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="417-430"}

::suggestion{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="423-425"}
        func formatStudiesText(appName: String) -> String {
            return String(format: strings.detailTextStudiesV2, appName)
        }

`labelStudiesV2`, `detailTextStudiesV2`, `labelRollouts`, `detailTextRollouts`, `detailTextSendUsageDataV2`, and the `SettingsTextFormatter` class have no references anywhere in the repo. `SettingsViewController` still reads the v1 `labelStudies` and `detailTextStudies`. This may be intentional for a base PR, but unused constants and a singleton are easy to forget and hard to review in isolation. The helper is the most misleading part, given the previous finding.

::diff{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="202-209"}

If the wiring lands in #30988, consider adding these constants and the helper there alongside the call site.
